The packages under sandbox/compat/daytona and sandbox/compat/modal mirror the
public Go API of two vendor SDKs, so that code written for them can run on
DigitalOcean Sandboxes after an import change.

  sandbox/compat/daytona  Daytona Go SDK
      github.com/daytonaio/daytona/libs/sdk-go v0.190.0
      (and its api-client-go and toolbox-api-client-go v0.190.0)
      Licensed under the Apache License 2.0: see LICENSE.daytona.

  sandbox/compat/modal    Modal Go SDK
      github.com/modal-labs/modal-client/go v0.11.2
      Licensed under the Apache License 2.0: see LICENSE.modal.

What is mirrored:
  - Type, constant and function declarations, and method signatures, as in the
    vendor packages. The files named zz_generated.go, types.go in apiclient and
    toolbox, and (in Daytona) errors/errors.go, options/options.go and
    types/types.go, are produced from the vendor sources by
    internal/gen. They keep the vendor's declarations; the method bodies are
    DigitalOcean code.
  - modal/errors.go and daytona/errors/errors.go, options/options.go and
    types/types.go are copied from the vendor sources with import paths
    changed. Their original copyright and license headers are kept where the
    vendor had them.

The vendor SDKs are not dependencies of godo: nothing here imports them.
All other code in this directory is part of godo and is under godo's license.
